### Threat 5 — Social Engineering at Layer 1

| Technique | Description | Control |
|---|---|---|
| **Tailgating / Piggybacking** | Following an authorised person through a secure door without badging | Mantraps, security awareness training, challenge culture |
| **Shoulder Surfing** | Watching someone type credentials in a public space | Privacy screens, awareness training, body positioning |
| **Pretexting** | Fabricating a scenario to gain physical access ("I'm from IT") | Visitor verification procedures, escort policy, staff training |
| **Dumpster Diving** | Recovering sensitive info from discarded materials | Secure document shredding policy, locked bins |

> 🎓 **CompTIA Security+ — Social Engineering Controls**
>
> - **Mantrap** — two-door entry system that prevents tailgating (first door must close before second opens)
> - **Security awareness training** — most effective control for social engineering
> - **Clean desk policy** — nothing sensitive left visible or accessible
> - **Privacy screens** — prevents shoulder surfing on laptops in public spaces

