### Threat 6 — Mobile Device Threats

Mobile devices are Layer 1 endpoints that travel outside the physical security perimeter constantly.

| Mobile threat | What happens | Why it matters to SOC | Control |
|---|---|---|---|
| Lost or stolen device | Attacker has full physical access to corporate data | Immediate data breach risk | MDM remote wipe |
| Malicious charging cable (O.MG Cable) | Hidden implant acts as BadUSB or creates Wi-Fi backdoor | Identical to legitimate cables — extremely hard to detect visually | Policy: only approved/labelled cables |
| SIM swapping | Attacker transfers phone number to their SIM | Bypasses SMS-based MFA — attacker receives all OTPs | Move to authenticator apps (TOTP) or hardware tokens |
| Juice jacking | Public USB charging point modified to install malware | Employees charging at airports, hotels — unaware of risk | AC adapters only; USB data blockers |
| Unapproved app installation | App with excessive permissions or malware | May exfiltrate corporate data, access camera/microphone | MDM app allowlisting; block sideloading |
| Jailbroken / rooted device | Security controls removed — MDM may be bypassed | Device may access corporate network completely unmanaged | MDM jailbreak detection; block non-compliant devices |

