## Chapter 4: SOC Skills — Layer 1 Investigations

### Investigation Workflow — Physical Security Incident

1. Alert fires: Splunk detects a new unrecognised MAC address on the 10.10.10.x network segment
2. Check asset inventory: Is this MAC address in the known asset list? What device type?
3. Check Zeek `conn.log`: What is this IP connecting to? What ports? How much data?
4. Check OPNsense DHCP leases: When did this device first appear? What name did it register?
5. Check physical access logs: Any badge swipes to network access areas at the same time?
6. Check CCTV if available: Any unescorted visitors or unfamiliar personnel?
7. Escalate: Unknown device + after-hours badge swipe + large data transfer = potential rogue device incident

### Layer 1 IoCs — Indicators of Compromise

| IoC type | What it looks like | Where you find it | Severity |
|---|---|---|---|
| New unregistered MAC address | MAC not in asset inventory appears on network | Zeek conn.log, OPNsense DHCP, Splunk | 🔴 HIGH |
| USB device event — new hardware | EID 6416 — unknown device connected | Sysmon / Windows Event Log / Splunk | 🟡 MEDIUM |
| Process execution from removable drive | EID 1 — executable launched from D:\ or E:\ | Sysmon / Splunk | 🔴 HIGH |
| After-hours badge swipe to restricted area | Physical access log entry outside business hours | Physical access control / SIEM | 🔴 HIGH |
| MDM jailbreak detection | Device security model bypassed | MDM platform / SIEM | 🔴 CRITICAL |
| MDM compliance failure | Device accessing network without required controls | MDM platform / SIEM | 🟡 MEDIUM |
| Rogue Wi-Fi SSID detected | Duplicate or spoofed corporate SSID | Wireless IDS / Zeek 802.11 | 🔴 HIGH |
| Geolocation anomaly | Device in unexpected location vs badge/login | MDM + SIEM correlation | 🔴 HIGH |

### Splunk Detection Queries

```spl
# Detect new USB device connections
index=wineventlog EventCode=6416
| table _time, host, DeviceName, DeviceId
| sort -_time

# Detect process execution from removable media
index=sysmon EventCode=1
| regex Image="^[D-Z]:\\"
| table _time, host, Image, CommandLine, User

# Detect new MAC addresses / IPs on network (last 24 hours)
index=zeek sourcetype=zeek_conn
| stats earliest(_time) as first_seen by id.orig_h
| where first_seen > relative_time(now(), "-1d@d")
```

> ✅ **Portfolio Tip**
>
> Document each query with: what it detects, why it matters, the MITRE technique it covers.
> In interviews, a Splunk dashboard showing Layer 1 IoC detection is a strong differentiator.
> Most candidates talk about network attacks — physical layer awareness stands out.

