## Chapter 6: Security Frameworks — Layer 1 Controls

### Controls Matrix

| Security control | Why it addresses Layer 1 | NIST SP | ISO 27001 | ACSC / APRA |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Physical access controls (locks, mantraps, badges) | Prevent unauthorised physical access | SP 800-116 | A.11.1.1 | APRA CPS 234 §36 |
| CCTV and security monitoring | Detect and deter physical intrusion | SP 800-53 PE-6 | A.11.1.2 | APRA CPS 234 §36 |
| Removable media controls (USB blocking) | Prevent USB drop attacks and insider exfiltration | SP 800-111 | A.8.3.1 | Essential Eight ML2 |
| Full disk encryption (BitLocker / FileVault) | Stolen device is unreadable without encryption key | SP 800-111 | A.10.1.1 | Essential Eight ML2 |
| Mobile Device Management (MDM) | Remote wipe, encryption enforcement, jailbreak detection | SP 800-124r2 | A.6.2.1 | Essential Eight ML2 |
| Hardware security audits | Detect rogue devices, keyloggers, unauthorised hardware | SP 800-53 PE-18 | A.11.2.4 | APRA CPS 234 §35 |
| Clean desk and clear screen policy | Prevent shoulder surfing and information exposure | SP 800-53 PE-5 | A.11.2.9 | ISM Control 0429 |
| Visitor management and escort policy | Prevent tailgating and social engineering | SP 800-53 PE-2 | A.11.1.2 | APRA CPS 234 §36 |
| Secure hardware disposal | Prevent data recovery from decommissioned equipment | SP 800-88r1 | A.11.2.7 | ISM Control 0363 |
| Network port security (disable unused ports) | Prevent rogue device connection to live network ports | SP 800-53 CM-7 | A.13.1.1 | Essential Eight ML2 |

### Australian Regulatory Context

> ✅ **What comes up in Australian SOC interviews**
>
> **Privacy Act 1988 / NDB scheme:**
> A stolen unencrypted laptop containing customer data is a **notifiable data breach**.
> SOC analysts may be involved in the investigation and 30-day notification process.
>
> **APRA CPS 234:**
> Financial institutions must protect information assets from physical threats.
> Physical access controls to systems handling customer financial data are in scope.
>
> **ACSC Essential Eight:**
> Application Control (ML2) covers restricting USB/removable media execution.
> Patch Applications and OS (ML2) — MDM enforces this on mobile endpoints.
>
> Knowing the regulatory consequence of a Layer 1 breach distinguishes a compliance-aware SOC analyst from a purely technical one.

