### Key Exam Terms

| Term | Definition | Exam context |
|---|---|---|
| Tailgating / piggybacking | Following an authorised person through a secure door | CompTIA's preferred term is tailgating |
| Mantrap | Two-door entry — first must close before second opens | Physical control — tested in Security Architecture |
| BadUSB | USB device identifying as HID/keyboard to execute commands | Firmware-level — antivirus cannot detect it |
| Juice jacking | Compromised public USB charging point | Defence: AC adapters or USB data blockers |
| MDM | Software for remotely managing enrolled mobile devices | Remote wipe, compliance enforcement, cert deployment |
| MAM | Managing applications only — not the whole device | Used in BYOD where full device management is inappropriate |
| BYOD | Policy allowing personal devices for work | Security trade-off: flexibility vs reduced SOC control |
| Containerisation | Separating corporate data into encrypted container on personal device | MDM manages only the container — personal data untouched |
| Full disk encryption (FDE) | Encrypting entire storage device | BitLocker (Windows), FileVault (Mac), LUKS (Linux) |
| Faraday cage | Enclosure blocking electromagnetic signals | Isolates high-value devices from RF exploitation |

